<title>BELGIUM: EU re-examines 1996/97 beet sugar figures.</title>
<headline>EU re-examines 1996/97 beet sugar figures.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission is re-examining European Union beet sugar figures supplied by individual member states showing output totalling 16.2 million tonnes in 1996/97, an EU official said.</p>
<p>In December, production was put at 15.9 million tonnes.</p>
<p>&quot;The figures clearly contain inconsistencies which need to be corrected,&quot; the official said, adding this also applied to 1995/96 data.</p>
<p>Total production for 1995/96 is unofficially reported to be 16.4 million tonnes -- 11.7 million of A quota, 2.4 million of B quota and 2.3 million of C (non-quota) sugar.</p>
<p>The figures will be discussed on Monday with the EU's sugar advisory committee, including trade and industry delegates. The meeting has been brought forward from March.</p>
<p>A more accurate sugar balance sheet is expected to be presented at the next sugar management committee on February 5.</p>
</text>
